# Forward references — paths a specification names that a later phase creates.
#
# `encorebom docs lint` treats these as expected-absent rather than broken.
# Format:  <repo-relative path>  # phase N — why
#
# A path may stay listed after it exists; the linter only uses this to suppress
# a not-found error, never to require absence.
#
# ADDING TO THIS FILE IS A DECISION, NOT A WORKAROUND. If a reference is here
# because the target was renamed or never planned, fix the reference instead.

libs/go-shared/model/certinid.go   # phase 1 — CERT-In identifier derivation
docs/RUNBOOKS.md                   # phase 16 — expanded from 08-OPERATIONS §6
services/report/internal/export/mlbom.go  # phase 12 owed — CycloneDX 1.6 ML-BOM export
